# What a server build does not need.
#
# A server build is the package, the lockfile, the tsconfigs and `src2`, so
# `ios/` and `android/` are left out by not being named at all. `src2` travels
# whole, though, and `export-ignore` is what keeps the parts of it only a Mac
# has any use for out of the archive.
#
# The **packages** they need are a different question and cannot be solved
# here: the server install is a plain `npm ci`, and it has to be, because the
# server starts through `sucrase` from `devDependencies`. So the native
# packages do install on the server. See `src2/MOBILE.md` for what that costs.
src2/maestro   export-ignore
src2/tools     export-ignore
